---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Thousand Sons Beginner's Guide — Warhammer 40k"
  description="New to Thousand Sons? Learn who they are, how the psychic shooting army plays, how to paint the iconic blue and gold scheme, and what to buy first."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#2a2a35]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/factions/" class="text-sm text-[#4a4855] hover:text-[#8a8590] transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">
        ← All Factions
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
        <div class="text-6xl">🔮</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#c9a84c] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 font-display">Faction Guide</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Thousand Sons</h1>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            They were the greatest scholars in the Space Marine legions. 
            Then their own sorcery destroyed them from within. 
            Now their armor marches on — hollow, ensorcelled, and utterly loyal to Tzeentch, 
            the Chaos god of magic and change.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick stats bar -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Playstyle</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Psychic Control</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Painting</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Rules</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-red-400">Hard</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Starter Cost</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">~$170</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lore -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">Who are the Thousand Sons?</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg">
        <p>
          The XV Legion were the scholars of the Space Marines. Where other legions trained for 
          war, the Thousand Sons obsessed over knowledge, sorcery, and the mysteries of the warp. 
          Their primarch, Magnus the Red, was a one-eyed giant of terrifying psychic ability — 
          arguably the most powerful psyker in human history, and possibly in all history.
        </p>
        <p>
          Their tragedy begins with good intentions. Magnus saw the Horus Heresy coming 
          and tried to warn the Emperor — sending a psychic message across the galaxy. 
          The message worked. But the act of sending it accidentally tore apart the Emperor's 
          secret project beneath the Imperial Palace, a gate into the warp he had been 
          building for years. The Emperor, furious, declared Magnus a traitor and sent the 
          Space Wolves to bring him in dead or alive.
        </p>
        <p>
          Faced with destruction, Magnus made a deal with Tzeentch — the Chaos god of change, 
          fate, and sorcery — and transported his entire planet into the Eye of Terror. 
          The legion survived. But something terrible was already consuming them: a 
          mutation caused by uncontrolled psychic power, slowly turning warriors to dust inside 
          their own armor.
        </p>
        <p>
          Ahriman, the legion's greatest sorcerer, cast a ritual called the Rubric of Ahriman 
          to stop the mutation. It worked — after a fashion. Every Thousand Sons warrior 
          without psychic ability was reduced to ash, their consciousness sealed forever 
          inside their armor. The Rubric Marines are hollow suits of power armor, marching 
          and firing because a soul is bound inside them. They follow orders. They feel nothing.
        </p>
        <p>
          Ahriman was exiled for what he did. Magnus still hasn't forgiven him. 
          The legion wanders the galaxy on schemes within schemes, serving Tzeentch — 
          who set all of this in motion, and finds it funny.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Playstyle -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">How they play on the table</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg mb-10">
        <p>
          Thousand Sons are a <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">psychic shooting army</strong> — 
          they advance methodically, layer buffs from their sorcerers, and unleash precise, 
          powerful ranged attacks. They are not a horde. You'll usually have fewer models 
          than your opponent, but yours will be significantly harder to kill and more effective per model.
        </p>
        <p>
          Their army rule is the <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Cabal of Sorcerers</strong> — 
          each turn your Sorcerer models can perform Rituals that grant powerful effects: 
          boosting your shooting, manipulating movement, or debuffing the enemy. 
          Managing which sorcerer performs which ritual, and in what order, is the core skill 
          of playing the army.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Rubric Marines</strong> are the backbone — 
          durable, self-sufficient infantry with solid shooting. 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Tzaangors</strong> are cheaper, more numerous units 
          that provide bodies for objective holding and melee screening. 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Exalted Sorcerers</strong> lead and enable your 
          whole army, so protecting them matters enormously.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is an army that rewards careful positioning and planning several turns ahead. 
          It's one of the higher skill-ceiling factions in the game — not ideal if you want 
          to pick up and play without much thought, but deeply rewarding once it clicks.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-green-400">Thousand Sons are for you if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✓ You want to out-think your opponent, not just out-punch them</li>
            <li>✓ You love the Egyptian / sorcerer aesthetic</li>
            <li>✓ You want a visually stunning, iconic paint scheme</li>
            <li>✓ You prefer smaller, elite armies over hordes</li>
            <li>✓ You enjoy reading into faction lore — this one goes deep</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-red-400">Maybe look elsewhere if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✗ You're completely new to the game and want a simple army</li>
            <li>✗ You prefer fast, aggressive melee</li>
            <li>✗ You want lots of cheap, expendable troops</li>
            <li>✗ You don't want to track multiple abilities and buffs each turn</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Painting -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">How to paint Thousand Sons</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        Blue armor and gold trim — one of the most iconic schemes in 40k. 
        It looks harder than it is. The blue is straightforward; the gold requires patience.
      </p>

      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 mb-10">
        <p>
          The Thousand Sons' blue is named after the faction — Citadel literally makes a paint 
          called Thousand Sons Blue. It's a rich, vivid tone that photographs beautifully and 
          looks striking in mass. The gold trim is the part that takes time: there's a lot of it, 
          it requires care to apply neatly, and it needs a wash to stop looking too flat and bright.
        </p>
        <p>
          The good news: even basic execution of this scheme looks excellent. 
          Blue and gold is forgiving in a way that, say, green or brown are not — 
          the contrast is strong enough that small mistakes disappear into the overall effect.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg mb-4">The classic scheme — step by step</h3>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Prime with Chaos Black spray</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Black primer gives the blue more depth and makes the gold pop harder by contrast. Standard black primer, fully dry before moving on.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Basecoat armor with Thousand Sons Blue</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Two thin coats over all the blue armor panels. This is the named Citadel layer paint — the color is exactly right for the classic scheme. Take your time; let each coat dry.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Wash blue armor with Drakenhof Nightshade</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A blue-tinted shade that flows into recesses and adds depth without muddying the color. Apply carefully to avoid pooling on flat surfaces — wipe with a clean damp brush if needed.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Drybrush with Ahriman Blue</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A lighter blue applied lightly across raised edges and armor plates. Brings the blue back to life after the dark wash and adds instant highlights without needing fine brushwork.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">5</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Basecoat all gold areas with Retributor Armour</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Trim, shoulder pad rims, helmet decorations, backpack detail — everything gold. Two thin coats for solid coverage. This takes time but it's the step that makes the model look Thousand Sons.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">6</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Wash gold with Reikland Fleshshade</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A warm shade that adds age and depth to the gold. Apply into recesses and let it pool slightly for a rich, ancient-looking metal. Wipe flat surfaces clean if needed.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">7</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Pick out weapon barrels and eye lenses</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Leadbelcher on gun barrels, washed Nuln Oil. Eye lenses: Liche Purple or Screamer Pink for a sorcerous glow — or bright Teclis Blue to match the armor tone. Either works.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">
          The most visually impactful step is actually step 5 — when the gold goes on, 
          the model transforms. Everything before is scaffolding.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- What to buy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">What to buy first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-10 text-lg">In order. Don't buy anything else until you've finished step one.</p>

      <!-- Combat Patrol -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
          <div>
            <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display mr-2">Start Here</span>
            <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$170</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Combat Patrol: Thousand Sons</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Contains a Daemon Prince (a powerful flying centrepiece), a Tzaangor Shaman (a 
          character who leads your Tzaangor units), 3 Tzaangor Enlightened (fast, 
          mobile cavalry-style models), and 10 Rubric Marines (your core infantry — 
          the hollow suits that define the army). 15 models total. A legal, playable 
          force out of one box.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0F8BVJ69F?tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          See price on Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Expansion -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$55 · natural first expansion</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Rubric Marines (box of 10)</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          More Rubric Marines means more reliable, durable shooting and more bodies on 
          the table — which the Thousand Sons always want. The kit also includes an 
          Aspiring Sorcerer to lead the squad and a choice of weapon options. 
          The right next box if you want to expand your core infantry.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=rubric+marines+warhammer+40k+thousand+sons&tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Paints -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Paints you need</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'Chaos Black Spray', use: 'Primer — gives the blue its depth', required: true },
            { name: 'Thousand Sons Blue', use: 'Base armor color — named after the faction', required: true },
            { name: 'Drakenhof Nightshade', use: 'Blue shade wash — adds depth to armor recesses', required: true },
            { name: 'Ahriman Blue', use: 'Drybrush highlight on armor panels', required: true },
            { name: 'Retributor Armour', use: 'All the gold trim and decoration', required: true },
            { name: 'Reikland Fleshshade', use: 'Warm shade wash over the gold', required: true },
            { name: 'Leadbelcher', use: 'Weapon barrels and metal details', required: true },
            { name: 'Nuln Oil', use: 'Shade wash for metal areas', required: true },
            { name: 'Teclis Blue', use: 'Optional highlight on armor edges and lenses', required: false },
            { name: 'Astrogranite Debris', use: 'Texture paint for basing', required: false },
          ].map(paint => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class={`text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 font-display ${paint.required ? 'bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113]' : 'border border-[#2a2a35] text-[#4a4855]'}`}>
                {paint.required ? 'Essential' : 'Optional'}
              </span>
              <div>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold">{paint.name}</span>
                <span class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm"> — {paint.use}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Edition note -->
  <section class="px-6 py-12 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
        <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-[#8a8590]">Edition note:</strong> Warhammer 40,000 releases new editions periodically — 
          specific rules, points costs, and detachment abilities change between them. 
          The lore, models, and painting guides on this page are edition-agnostic. 
          For current rules, check the <a href="https://wahapedia.ru/wh40k10ed/factions/thousand-sons/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-[#c9a84c] hover:underline">Thousand Sons rules on Wahapedia</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 text-center">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold mb-4">All is dust.</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg mb-8">
        Not sure Thousand Sons are right for you? Take the quiz — it matches you to a faction 
        based on how you actually want to play.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a
          href="/quiz"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display tracking-wide"
        >
          Take the Faction Quiz →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/factions/"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display"
        >
          All Factions
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
